; primitive-edge-contracts-band.fk — the bounds-checked accessors answer the same
; thing on every arm, including at the edges where the natives part company.
;
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/core.fk observe/primitive-edge-contracts.fk
;
; Band verdict 1023 when every claim lands (1+2+...+512):
;   1    in range, pec-substring is the native's answer
;   2    past the end it clamps rather than dying
;   4    an inverted window is empty, not an error
;   8    a negative start clamps to 0
;   16   in range, pec-char-at is the native's answer
;   32   past the end pec-char-at is empty
;   64   a negative index is empty
;   128  pec-byte-at answers -1 outside the text and the real byte inside it, so a
;        caller can tell "no byte here" from "the byte is 0"
;   256  a walk deliberately run four bytes past the end terminates and yields the
;        whole string — the shape that silently truncates on fkwu and dies on the
;        other three when written against the raw natives
;   512  the recorded divergence table is intact: 22 probes run, 15 agreed, 7 did not
;
; This band never calls a native out of range. That is the point: it is runnable on
; all four arms precisely because the vocabulary it proves keeps the natives inside
; their declared contract.
;
; PERTURBATION, AND THE REASON THIS NEEDS FOUR ARMS. Take the clamp out of
; pec-substring — replace both `(pec-clamp ...)` with the bare argument — and run again:
;
;   fkwu  1023   (unchanged: its native clamps too, so the check was never doing work)
;   go    dies   rust  dies   ts  dies
;
; **On fkwu the safety code is invisible.** The band cannot tell whether the bounds
; check is present, because the native underneath already answers the same way. Only
; the other three arms can show the clamp is load-bearing, and they show it by dying
; without it. That is an argument for the four-way that has nothing to do with
; agreement: a second kernel is not only a witness against a wrong answer, it is the
; only thing that can prove a guard is doing anything at all.

(do
    (add
        (add
            (add
                (if (str_eq (pec-substring "abcdef" 1 4) "bcd") 1 0)
                (if (str_eq (pec-substring "abc" 1 99) "bc") 2 0))
            (add
                (if (str_eq (pec-substring "abc" 2 1) "") 4 0)
                (if (str_eq (pec-substring "abc" (sub 0 1) 2) "ab") 8 0)))
        (add
            (add
                (add
                    (if (str_eq (pec-char-at "abc" 1) "b") 16 0)
                    (if (str_eq (pec-char-at "abc" 9) "") 32 0))
                (add
                    (if (str_eq (pec-char-at "abc" (sub 0 3)) "") 64 0)
                    (if (and (eq (pec-byte-at "abc" 0) 97)
                             (and (eq (pec-byte-at "abc" 9) (sub 0 1))
                                  (eq (pec-byte-at "abc" (sub 0 1)) (sub 0 1)))) 128 0)))
            (add
                (if (str_eq (pec-collect-overrun "abcdef" 4) "abcdef") 256 0)
                (if (and (eq (pec-probes-run) 22)
                         (and (eq (pec-probes-agreeing) 15)
                              (eq (pec-edge-count) 7))) 512 0)))))
